bio informatics for procedure oncology  is an online training program that is  going to cover a number of topics  related to precision oncology we will  explore how next-generation sequencing  including genomic mutations and gene  expression profiling are being utilized  in oncology research today many of these  techniques rely on bioinformatics so we  will explore how this program can help  anyone developed an independent project  in a fully online environment we will be  meeting bi-weekly every Monday and  Thursday the meetings will be online and  will last about an hour and the program  will last between June 10th and August  30th in 2019 our program speakers and  trainers include experienced  bioinformaticians as well as biologists  that have been conducting research for a  number of years they will introduce the  topics and cover the hands-on component  of every aspect so that it will be easy  to follow for a novice and expert alike  our first session will be dedicated to  the introduction to precision oncology  in this session we will talk about how  cancer occurs which biological changes  in organs tissues and cells cause cancer  and how cancer develops will also  discuss molecular factors in tumor  development and growth and metastasis we  will take a look at how clinical and  molecular data can be combined to really  understand this complex disease then we  will talk about the big data  bioinformatics how big data and  bioinformatics methods have made the  statistical approach to the analysis of  molecular data different we will talk  about the transition between hypothesis  testing which is a guided or supervised  type of analysis to data mining an  unsupervised type of analysis we will  also talk about very statistical aspects  and algorithmic aspects of analysis and  the different approaches to the  challenges that big data  and we'll also learn about the tee  violin for platform environment where we  will take various methods that require a  long time to run and also a long time to  design to run on your own computer that  way anyone even a novice can use the  point-and-click interface and understand  the logic of how these methods work  together to produce the desired result  we will also talk about the processing  of data identification of germline and  somatic mutations from genomic or DNA  data we'll also talk about the analysis  of this initial process data to  accurately detect variants and then we  will talk about interpretation how to  detect driver mutations oncogenes and  how to compile this information from the  whole genome we will also look at the  gene expression profiling how the  message of processing such as mapping  and quantification analysis such as  differential gene expression factor  regression analysis and others as well  as interpretation using gene ontology x'  and gene sets like pathways could be  used to really understand the biology of  a given sample we will also cover data  sources and databases taking a look at  NCBI repositories like TCGA and  reference databases compiled by  organizations like the National Cancer  Institute or cosmic finally we will talk  about some of the open questions and  some of the ways projects in  bioinformatics are typically designed  and how those projects could be compiled  into a proposal we will talk about  scientific inquiry and translational  value various aspects of cancer and look  at several examples including breast  cancer and liver cancer we are excited  to announce the registration for  introduction to precision oncology  starting immediately our program  speakers include Justin door who holds a  PhD in molecular biology from Brandeis  University as well as ProTeam  Chakraborty  who has a PhD in bioinformatics Sahil  Sethi who holds a master's degree in  biomedical informatics and we'll heat  Mazumdar who holds a PhD in  computational biology throughout this  program we will also rely on resources  available on the educational tion for  platform it will go together through  some of the basic courses like  introduction to bioinformatics  transcriptomics 1 in genomics 1 and look  at some of the projects that are  available for oncology research projects  like modeling cancer precision medicine  or a look at exercise in the DCIS  exosomes early stage breast cancer  biomarkers throughout the program all  the participants will have access to the  T bio info platform that combines easy  processing of data as well as analysis  visualization and interpretation at the  end of the program all of the  participants will get a certificate of  participation the program costs 135  dollars and will last for two and a half  months this includes a three months  training program hands-on analysis  practice one on one question answer  sessions as well as assistance 5  terabytes of data storage in a 14-day  account on T bio info you can register  at the link below  edu T bio infocomm forward slash  precision - oncology
 

